<Base title="Before You Give: privacy" description="What the Charitology browser extension reads, stores and sends.">
  <header class="page-head"><div class="wrap"><Crumbs items={[{label:'Tools',href:'/tools/'},{label:'Browser Extension',href:'/tools/browser-extension/'},{label:'Privacy'}]} /><h1>Before You Give: privacy</h1><p class="lede">No analytics, accounts, donation handling or background data transmission. Your checklist and search run locally.</p></div></header>
  <article class="wrap section-tight prose">
    <p>Applies to extension version 0.1.2. Updated October 27, 2026.</p>
    <h2>What it reads</h2><p>The toolbar popup reads the active tab’s title when you open it, to suggest a search. You can change or remove the suggestion. On supported URLs, the card reads the title when you click <em>Look it up</em>. It does not read donation amounts, payment details, form entries or account credentials.</p>
    <h2>What it stores</h2><p>Extension-local storage remembers the sites where you chose to hide the card. If that preference cannot be saved, the card says so and offers Close for the current page. Checked checklist boxes and search text are not saved by the extension. Removing the extension removes its local settings.</p>
    <h2>What happens when you click a link</h2><p>The extension opens a page on Charitology. A suggested search travels in the URL fragment after <code>#q=</code>; the browser does not include that fragment in its HTTP request. The lookup reads it locally. Suggested and manual queries are bounded to 120 characters. The name reaches an external registry only if you choose a registry link that includes the name. The lookup explains which links do this.</p>
    <p>Opening any website still sends an ordinary page request to its host, which receives information such as the requested path and IP address. Charitology is hosted on GitHub Pages; <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a> describes its hosting practices. Earlier extension version 0.1.0 used a query parameter, which was included in the page request.</p>
    <h2>Permissions</h2><ul><li><code>activeTab</code>: reads the current tab’s title when you open the popup.</li><li><code>storage</code>: remembers hidden sites locally.</li><li>Content-script matches: display the card on the supported GoFundMe, JustGiving and Every.org pages listed in the manifest.</li></ul>
    <h2>Check the code or report a problem</h2><p><a href={url('/tools/browser-extension/compatibility/')}>Exact URLs, compatibility limits and package checksums</a>.</p><p>The <a href={`${SITE.repo}/tree/main/extension`}>source is public</a>. Report a privacy issue through the <a href={`${SITE.repo}/issues/new?labels=extension`}>extension issue page</a>. You can also <a href={url('/tools/browser-extension/')}>read the installation instructions</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
